WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.100
- So dry out here.

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.770
Hi, I'm Garrett.
- And I'm Niki.

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:04.530
- We're fascinated by
how other people live.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:05.363
- [Niki] So we're gonna try and find

00:00:05.363 --> 00:00:06.810
some really interesting living situations.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.010
- [Garrett] And live there, experiencing

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.180
a totally different lifestyle.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.850
- [Niki] To see which ones
will bring us closer together.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.130
- [Garrett] Or push us further apart.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:14.110
- This week, we're living in Arcosanti.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:16.617
- It's really hard to explain.

00:00:16.617 --> 00:00:18.802
But you're gonna get the gist of it.

00:00:18.802 --> 00:00:21.385
(upbeat music)

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.830
- [Niki] Hello.
- [All] Hi!

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.280
- [Niki] I'm Niki.
- Hi Niki, nice to meet you.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.169
- Hi, Garrett.
- Shannon.

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:38.510
- Nice to meet you, Shannon.
- Nice to meet you, Shannon.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:39.730
- [Garrett] Thank you for having us at.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.756
- Absolutely.
- Arcosanti.

00:00:41.756 --> 00:00:43.440
- [Shannon] Absolutely.
- Which is.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.273
(record scratch)

00:00:44.273 --> 00:00:47.260
- Arcosanti, what is it?
- [Garrett] I don't know.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.230
- [Jeff] Arcosanti is trying

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.900
to demonstrate something,
how to build a city

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.920
as a totally integrated, single structure.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.570
- In the early 50's,
60's, 70's, there were

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.457
a lot of people who tried to start like,

00:01:00.457 --> 00:01:04.010
idealized societies and this is that.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.477
- [Shannon] Essentially, we are proving

00:01:06.477 --> 00:01:09.410
that you can live a rich life

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.570
without necessarily being rich

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.280
and without living in a development

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.040
that is negatively impactful on the earth.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.490
These are the vaulted arches.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.500
So this is essentially our city center.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.905
We meet here every morning
during the week as a community.

00:01:22.905 --> 00:01:25.071
- They've really thought very practically

00:01:25.071 --> 00:01:27.883
about how to live in a
community in a space.

00:01:27.883 --> 00:01:32.590
- The notion of community is
one that we have temporarily

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.670
lost in America and it's one that we hope

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.557
Arcosanti can serve as kindof a trigger

00:01:37.557 --> 00:01:39.250
for recovering.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:42.000
- [Shannon] The entire
structure here was built

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.720
by the people who live here.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.010
There is a fluctuating population.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.450
Around 60 to 80 people depending

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.960
on how big our workshops are.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.980
- I think it's like a work live situation

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.380
where everybody lives there also works

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.054
and maybe helps build it
or tends to the plants

00:01:57.054 --> 00:01:59.470
or makes bells.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.860
- [Shannon] This one in
particular is our ceramic studio

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:06.200
where we make the famous
ceramic soleri wind bells.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.040
The structure behind us is an apt shape

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:10.910
for it's passive solar heating
and cooling techniques.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:13.670
The sun, during the winter,
will pass much lower

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:15.998
in the sky so this
entire concrete structure

00:02:15.998 --> 00:02:18.450
will be filled with
sunlight, heating the air

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.941
inside the structure
as much as 15 degrees.

00:02:20.941 --> 00:02:21.774
- Whoa.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.240
- So the bells fund the architecture

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.870
which supports more manufacturing

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:30.020
which sortof, so it's like
this independent little city.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.633
- A little bit, yeah, to take
part in the Arcosanti project,

00:02:32.633 --> 00:02:36.040
you participate in a five week workshop

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.850
which takes you through
the history of Arcosanti

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.660
and then for the last three
weeks of your workshop,

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.320
you come back here and you participate

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.474
in one of the departments
within the foundation.

00:02:45.474 --> 00:02:47.690
Typically, people go into construction

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:48.982
which if you guys are up for it,

00:02:48.982 --> 00:02:51.910
we'll have you work in
construction tomorrow.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:54.280
- Awesome, here's the thing,
I have a masters degree

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.130
in sustainable design and construction

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.050
that I don't do anything with

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:59.690
but it will be interesting to see sortof

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:00.800
what's going on in that field

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.460
and what these people are doing.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.550
- The desert just seems
like a scary place to die.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:05.870
It seems like one of those places

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.446
where humans should
not be, but if we learn

00:03:08.446 --> 00:03:11.550
to live in the desert,
maybe that will be better.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.830
- So these are housing in here,

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.089
these are houses in here.

00:03:15.089 --> 00:03:16.589
- [Niki] That's housing?
- That's housing.

00:03:16.589 --> 00:03:18.090
That's housing.
- [Garrett] Can I ask how much

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.516
like one of the spaces would rent is?

00:03:20.516 --> 00:03:22.320
- It's $300 a month.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.660
- What?
- $300 a month?

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.973
- Yep.
- Wow.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.910
I don't think Niki's going to like this.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:31.170
Niki doesn't like meeting new people

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.700
